  "body": "Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy allows websites to request being put in browsing context groups containing only top level documents from their origin. We think it is needed to deploy several powerful features that would create side-channels exploitable by bad actors without the extra-isolation COOP (+COEP) provides.\r\n\r\nAt the same time, COOP breaks opener relationships, and may cause breakages to websites when deployed. We'd like to introduce a reporting API for Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy that helps developers with their COOP deployment. In particular, we would like to have a report-only mode similar to CSP that developers can use to learn about potential breakages with COOP before deploying COOP on their site.\r\n\r\nI created an explainer [here](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zWqwI8PFrezwQpBSejIMUfdtsIYl9-h8epasdrDXVIM/edit?usp=sharing).\r\n\r\ncc @whatwg/cross-origin-isolation ",
